ne It is presented as a \plain \f24 \b shareware\plain \f24 , created by \plain \f24 \b Pierre VERNAY\plain \f24 , on a Psion 3A (2Mo, and with DataViewPro and JBData softwares), between May 97 and May 99.\line The version distributed usually is not a trial version, but just the first third of the database, including the Directors from \plain \f24 \b A \plain \f24 (ABBOTT George) to \plain \f24 \b F \plain \f24 (FURIE Sidney J.) only. Those interested in the complete version, from \plain \f24 \b A \plain \f24 to \plain \f24 \b Z\plain \f24 , should read the chapter "\plain \f24 \b How to register\plain \f24 " of this text.\line \plain \f24 \b It can be used on any type of computer \plain \f24 (Psion 3 or 5, Mac and PC, etc.), as long as you have a database program.\par \pard \plain \s28 \qj \sa240 \sl360 \tx720 \tx1440 \tx2160 \tx2880 \tx3600 \tx4320 \tx5040 \tx5760 \f24 \b \ul Presentation.\plain \f24 \line This database is also distributed in French under the name CINEPHIL, since "Cin\'82phile" means "Moviefan".\par \pard \plain \s28 \qj \sa240 \sl360 \tx720 \tx1440 \tx2160 \tx2880 \tx3600 \tx4320 \tx5040 \tx5760 \f24 In its present and future states, my database will not attempt to be a complete or universal reference, since it is based mostly on films I have seen myself.\line It only corresponds to a need I've had since the beginning of my "\plain \f24 \b CINEPHIL\plain \f24 ie" : to structure my memory and retain the contents in using a less volatile medium...\line The job's now done... What are two years of work compared to 30 years of "\plain \f24 \b cin\'82phil\plain \f24 ie" ???\par \pard \plain \s28 \qj \sa240 \sl360 \tx720 \tx1440 \tx2160 \tx2880 \tx3600 \tx4320 \tx5040 \tx5760 \f24 This database does contain a number of errors (typing, spelling and probably incorrect names), and it is far from being complete for a great number of films, but with time the succeeding versions will tend to be more exhaustive and accurate.\line Now it's up to everyone of you to use it in such a way you choose.\line There remains the problem of my personal findings (for those who are interested in translating them from the French original, of course...), which will undeniably annoy some readers, and be paradoxical to others...\line You must understand that, having made it for my own personal use, it is more than anything a mirror of my own analyses, evolving through the years, and it does only "engage" myself. It is up to you to "eliminate" whatever bothers you. \line One must also understand that it is the result of a "\plain \f24 \b cin\'82phil\plain \f24 ie" of some 32 years, and that my "critical filter" has had largely the time (and the need) to narrow, by viewing lots of good and bad movies (a necessary discomfort), and by watching again many of the good ones... as well as the bad.\line This is to explain the sometimes surprising differences between my first-time appreciation and the next, and to recognize that my appreciation "Bon" ("Good") often encountered in the database, hasn't much in common with my present vision : most of the time it would be replaced  by a definite "Very poor" for "Bon" or by "Appalling" for "Bon-"... and if I haven't made this adjustment, it is due to incertitude, laziness or leniency...\par \pard \plain \s28 \qj \sa240 \sl360 \tx720 \tx1440 \tx2160 \tx2880 \tx3600 \tx4320 \tx5040 \tx5760 \f24 \b \ul History.\plain \f24 \line I began my work in 1997, and released :\line - \plain \f24 \i Version 1 \plain \f24 of CINEPHIL in October 98, on the Psion French Club site (\plain \f24 \i http:/www.cabuzel.com/psion/index.html\plain \f24 ),\line - this version, \plain \f24 \i Version 2\plain \f24 , in May 99 with an equivalent English name : CINEFAN. Many corrections, and it has almost the same number of files, but it is notably heavier, due to additions within various fields. But there is still work to be done, which I reserve for \plain \f24 \i Version 3\plain \f24 ...\par \pard \plain \s28 \qj \sa240 \sl360 \tx720 \tx1440 \tx2160 \tx2880 \tx3600 \tx4320 \tx5040 \tx5760 \f24 \b \ul Installation and working on the base.\plain \f24 \line You should have found the base in a Zip-compressed format, and if you are reading this text, you must have already expanded it. Now you just have to put the base CINEFAN into the \plain \f24 \b DAT \plain \f24 directory of your Psion S3 (a, c or mx), or in its SSDFlash (if necessary, create there a \plain \f24 \b DAT \plain \f24 directory).\line Owners of a S3a like myself will be totally handicapped by the original Data application, which is much too limited.\line They might find an interest in installing software like \plain \f24 \b Dataview Pro \plain \f24 and/or \plain \f24 \b JBData \plain \f24 into their \plain \f24 \b APP \plain \f24 directory (either in the Psion itself or in one of its SSDFlash) , in order to open the base from one of those applications. Each option will have a specific and complementary efficiency (or play a part) on this base : \line - \plain \f24 \b Dataview Pro \plain \f24 (commercial software from Purple Software, site at www.3lib.ukonline.co.uk/dvpro.htm) offers a good list presentation, secondary groups and a good sorting. \line - \plain \f24 \b JBData \plain \f24 has the huge advantage of being freeware (a very big and respectful "Thank you" to John Boyce, its prolific and dedicated "father" ; site at www.3lib.ukonline.co.uk/~jbsoft/programs.htm). It allows an interesting "\plain \f24 \i Save as\plain \f24 " function on a Text format, plus good "\plain \f24 \i Replace\plain \f24 " and "\plain \f24 \i Merge\plain \f24 " functions.\line These two applications will be equally useful for happy owners of the S3c and especially the S3mx, who will thereby be able to profit from the new processor enhancements for sorting functions.\line Considering the present size of this CINEFAN (or CINEPHIL) base when complete (at least 2,2 Mb in .dbf psionS3 format), direct management from the hard disk is unfortunately impossible. Hence, one must work from a 4 Mb SSD Flash at least, while hoping that Psion offers us a model with a more consistant hard disk soon...\line S5 owners will not have that problem, and what's more they have at their disposal the new \plain \f24 \b Power Base\plain \f24  program (from Purple Software), which should provide very flexible management of this base. \line People will certainly want to insert their own files and reviews within my base : and indeed that should be the aim of the game... Considering the up-dates and improvements I'm planning to implement on the base, I would advise that you make a kind of parallel and distinct file for your own list, so you will not lose anything of your own base when replacing mine with a new version.\line Now, about the translation to a Text format, in order to use that base on a bigger computer (Mac or PC), through such softwares as Access, FileMaker or 4D : use \plain \f24 \b JBData \plain \f24 "\plain \f24 \i save as\plain \f24 " function : \line 1) Give a \plain \f24 \i name\plain \f24 \b .txt\plain \f24 \line 2) Leave "\plain \f24 \i Text\plain \f24 ", put "\plain \f24 \i Tab\plain \f24 " on the next field, insert or not your labels with "\plain \f24 \b \i Labels \plain \f24 \i : first record\plain \f24 ", and if you have used "Psion-Enter" to make new paragraphs within fields, put "\plain \f24 \i Leave\plain \f24 " on the bottom line. You should also refer to the JBData manual.\line On a next version, I will provide some keywords to replace my French abreviations with their equivalents in English, replacement to be made with JBData.\par \pard \plain \s28 \qj \sa240 \sl360 \tx720 \tx1440 \tx2160 \tx2880 \tx3600 \tx4320 \tx5040 \tx5760 \f24 \b \ul Registering this shareware.\plain \f24 \line The creation of such a database has taken, as one might imagine, a lot of work often enjoyabl